    {
      "id": "98rnkwu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Magnetism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6vjqng3",
      "content": "Magnetism is the property of materials that attract iron and other magnetic materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wnwirr6",
      "content": "Magnets have two poles: North pole and South pole."
    },
    {
      "id": "ny0qq9t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Properties of Magnets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hwgf9n4",
      "content": "• Like poles repel each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8n7vhyk",
      "content": "• Unlike poles attract each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "llz35qc",
      "content": "• Magnetic poles always exist in pairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0mion4a",
      "content": "• Magnetic force is strongest at the poles."
    },
    {
      "id": "hv6y5fb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Electromagnet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jw19n31",
      "content": "An electromagnet is a magnet produced by passing electric current through a coil of wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6q8pny3",
      "content": "Applications:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ohm's Law is valid only for ohmic conductors (metals) at constant temperature and fails for semiconductors and vacuum tubes.",
        "In series connections, electric current remains identical throughout, whereas voltage is identical across parallel branches.",
        "Soft iron is selected for electromagnet cores because of its high magnetic permeability and low retentivity."
      ],
      "id": "8p537m9"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "p70mtrv",
      "content": "• Electric bell"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ltgt58h",
      "content": "• Electric motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dcwo1rh",
      "content": "• Magnetic cranes"
    },
    {
      "id": "vevan7i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w8wl08o",
      "content": "• SI unit of electric current is Ampere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mfh28j7",
      "content": "• Ohm’s law formula is V = IR."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qdib9w9",
      "content": "• SI unit of resistance is Ohm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5rf1750",
      "content": "• Like poles repel and unlike poles attract."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}